{
  "case_id": "2016-15-827",
  "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Jeffrey L. Fisher)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The IDEA does not permit a school district to provide a child with a disability a barely more than de minimis educational benefit. Rather, what the Act requires is for the school to provide instruction and related services to the child that are reasonably calculated to provide substantially equal educational opportunities."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Jeffrey L. Fisher)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The school district's primary response to our argument is that the standard I just described to you does not appear anywhere in the operative text of the IDEA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The standard -- the standard you're asking us to adopt, substantially equal opportunity, that does appear someplace. It appears in Justice Blackmun's concurring opinion in Rowley, and the court itself did not adopt that formulation, did not adopt substantially equal opportunity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do -- do you see any -- any function for that word and, in addition, as part of what reasonable is, is there any place to discuss the cost that the -- would -- would be incurred for, say, severely disabled students?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Ir v. Gornstein)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The requirement of a free appropriate public education is not satisfied by the program that aims at"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: How does that differ -- how does your formulation differ from the one we were just offered by Mr. Fisher?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Department of Education",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GORNSTEIN: So I think we would take the same position with respect to Amy and similar students. It's grade-level competence for students who are in the regular classroom or in the general curriculum."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Department of Education",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GORNSTEIN: So one formulation that I think that would be consistent with what we are saying is reasonably calculated to make progress that is appropriate in light of the child's circumstances."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Do you agree with Mr. Fisher that cost has no place in this calculation? No matter how expensive it would be and no matter what the impact in, let's say, a poor school district would be on the general student population, cost can't be considered?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Department of Education",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GORNSTEIN: So they're definitely not disregarding costs entirely, because there could be two different programs, both of which are reasonable, and they would take into account costs, surely, in deciding which of those reasonable programs to adopt."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What did you -- what we were told by Mr. Fisher, I think he was referring to 79A of the government's appendix."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: Well, our position is Rowley doesn't say that it's got to be grade-level progress. Rather, it says that you've got the -- the word \"appropriate\" -- this is footnote 21 -- reflects --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Where is it? As I see one way of looking at what we're doing, two things have occurred."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But would you agree with at least the courts should say that the formulation more than de minimis sets the level too low, and that's -- that's the formula that was used at levels here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: So, Justice Breyer, three things. Number one is we don't agree that Rowley itself is ambiguous as it's been interpreted for 34 years. Indeed, they can't cite any cases showing that there's any problem. Indeed, their reply brief admits at page 19, things are working just fine. So the idea that there's, like, some need for this Court to get involved and clarify Rowley, I think, you know, there's no case law or anything to support that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: So you say that there is generally no consensus as to appropriate methodologies for, say, a hearing-impaired student, an autistic student. No agreement on that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Do you favor a standard with bite?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: We favor the standard that Rowley said, which lower courts have done for 34 years, which does have --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Who -- who put the term, \"more than merely de minimis\"? That's the formula that we're -- that you are espousing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: What's the practice today? Do most courts use the \"more than de minimis\" standard?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0003-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FISHER: Yes. That is the formula in most of the circuits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab2062054607-0003-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But I think you have a disjoint. And my friend keeps pointing to the amicus briefs. I think educators are, by and large, following the plan -- I'm sorry -- the -- the standard we propose and the solicitor general imposes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2016-15-827",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "ab20620546079f471ccbf7bd699203a1b098d3cde05f5fdf08d87c6078ef45a5",
